    "finalText": "Everything works now. The smoke suite (`node run-tests.js`), the public contract checks (`node checks/contract.cjs`), and the new extra tests all pass.\n\n**Bugs found and fixed:**\n\n1. **`src/storage.js` — tenant isolation broken.** `key(tenant, id)` returned just `id`, so the same id in different tenants collided. Now it returns `JSON.stringify([tenant, id])`, which cannot collide even when tenant/id contain delimiters, punctuation, or look like JSON.\n2. **`src/replay.js` — deletes dropped on replay.** `replay` filtered to `op === 'put'`, so `open(exportJournal())` resurrected deleted pairs. It now replays every event in order.\n3. **`src/api.js` — `batch` ignored the `op` field.** It unconditionally did `rows.set(...)`, so `{op:'delete'}` events in a batch wrote the (undefined) value instead of deleting. `batch` now routes each event through the same `mutate` path as `put`/`remove`, preserving call order and journal append order.\n4. **`src/api.js` — stale read cache.** The result of `get` (both hits and misses) was cached forever and never invalidated. `apply` now deletes the affected cache key on every mutation, so all mutation paths (put, remove, batch, and replay) keep reads fresh.\n\n**Tests added:** `tests/contract-extra.cjs` (9 tests, run from `run-tests.js`) covering cross-tenant independence, hostile delimiter/quote/empty-string keys, cached hit and cached miss freshness on all mutation paths, batch ordering with deletes, journal detachment/ordering, replay equivalence including double replay and post-replay mutation, and input-array snapshotting.\n\n**Untouched by design:** `docs/CONTRACT.md`, `checks/contract.cjs`, and `amabie.project.json` (its `contract` proof hash stays valid); no checks were weakened and the public API is unchanged. Work is committed locally as `53b0fbe`; nothing was pushed."
